    {
      "id": "gdy1oem",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Location and Extent"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The physical geography of Arunachal Pradesh is categorized into three major zones: the Outer Himalayan Zone (Siwalik Range), the Middle Himalayan Zone, and the Trans-Himalayan Zone (Greater Himalayas).",
        "Major mountain peaks and strategic high-altitude mountain passes (La) form critical geographical and historical boundaries.",
        "The state is characterized by complex river systems, distinct microclimates, and multiple administrative districts."
      ],
      "id": "locnxat"
    },
