    {
      "id": "0kexphd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.5 Climate"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jiri43r",
      "content": "The climate of Arunachal Pradesh is strongly influenced by altitude and topography. Due to the enormous variation in elevation, the state experiences almost all types of climates — from tropical in the south to tundra in the high north."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the distinction between Outer (Siwalik), Middle, and Trans-Himalayan (Greater) zones.",
        "Strategic mountain passes (La) and high-altitude peaks are common match-the-following questions in state competitive exams.",
        "River courses and regional climate variations across districts are important topics for objective questions."
      ],
      "id": "j54qd5p"
    },
