            "<p>Hot and humid tropical; rainfall 3,000–5,000 mm annually</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Middle Hills</strong></p>",
            "<p>Subtropical to temperate; moderate temperatures</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>High Mountains</strong></p>",
            "<p>Sub-alpine to alpine; heavy snowfall in winter</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Trans-Himalayan</strong></p>",
            "<p>Cold desert / tundra conditions; very low precipitation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Monsoon Season</strong></p>",
            "<p>June to September; accounts for 70–80% of annual rainfall</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Winter</strong></p>",
            "<p>November to February; snowfall above 2,000 m elevation</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "reigyyv",
      "content": "Cherrapunji-like rainfall is experienced in some districts. Daporijo (Upper Subansiri) and parts of Tirap receive over 4,000 mm of rainfall annually. The Tawang area in contrast is much drier due to rain shadow effects."
    },
    {
